    iio: inv_mpu6050: Document DMP ABI and core-owned scan layout
    
    Leave timestamp placement to the current core using a zero-initialized
    32-byte sample container. The introducing core places the timestamp at
    byte 16 with eight tail-padding bytes; the legacy 6.18 helper used byte
    24. Document the stream and one-shot event contracts, external firmware
    and suspend requirements. Add the ABI path to existing maintainership.
    
    Tidy alignment carried by the original feature patches. The complete
    candidate compiles 18 IIO/MPU/IADC objects on each of native Qualcomm ARM
    and ARM64 with W=1 and no diagnostics. Actual IIO helpers demonstrate
    both legacy and current layouts and reject the obsolete reader control.
    
    Generated with OpenAI Codex assistance; no firmware bytes are included.

